cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you implement or adopt E+, cite the version you implemented."
title: "E+ - Earth Health Score Methodology"
# CFF 1.2.0 allows only 'dataset' or 'software' at the top level. E+ is a
# standard; 'software' is the closest option the format offers, and it is the
# same choice CITATION.cff makes for AiEDs. GitHub reads only CITATION.cff, so
# this file is for humans and for tools pointed at it directly.
type: software
version: 1.1.0
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
repository-code: https://github.com/random-knights/standard
url: https://standard.rand0m.ai/eplus/v1/methodology.md
abstract: >-
  A 0 to 100 planetary health index built from nine environmental domains:
  weights, normalizers, the coverage-normalized region mean, the
  exposure-weighted headline, a five-rung provenance ladder that forbids
  claiming live for a synthetic input, a non-averageable breach panel with
  cited thresholds, and the conformance test that recomputes every published
  number from the published document alone. Version 1.1.0 is a DRAFT awaiting
  owner ratification; the canonical text is eplus/v1/methodology.md in this
  repository.
keywords:
  - Earth health score
  - planetary boundaries
  - open standard
authors:
  - name: "Random Knights, LLC"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-5066-1693"
    city: Roswell
    region: Georgia
    country: US
    website: https://randomknights.xyz
contact:
  - name: "Random Knights, LLC"
    email: knights@rand0m.ai
